    {
      "number": 2,
      "id": "I_kwDOMRm-Tc6O1_bW",
      "title": "Corey Mosher: Consider adding guidance for capabilities checking and compat tables for TLS, specifically caching of valid servers",
      "url": "https://github.com/ietf-wg-add/draft-ietf-add-Encrypted-DNS-Server-RedirectionEncDNSServerRedirect/issues/2",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "author": "mstojens",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [
        "Minor"
      ],
      "body": "Per the existing guidance to not use lesser encryption in a redirect chain, a mechanism for tracking which servers are suitable (or not) for redirection will need to be maintained to avoid JIT or per-connection suitable redirect target detection. This at least dictates that a small cache should be maintained. This is likely to be neighbor-only but could potentially be handled by following a proposed redirection chain to the end and storing values (including TTLs). Additionally, a server could potentially choose to short-cut known existing chains based on TTLs of all paths en-route to the terminal server and supply the terminal server to the client directly.\r\n\r\nI think this very much fits into the 'server considerations' discussion and we could slide in a client comment if we feel it necessary.",
      "createdAt": "2024-07-08T20:34:04Z",
      "updatedAt": "2024-10-21T18:39:17Z",
      "closedAt": "2024-10-21T18:39:17Z",
      "comments": []
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "id": "I_kwDOMRm-Tc6a4V-s",
      "title": "Med: could reuse RESINFO to advertise support for redirection",
      "url": "https://github.com/ietf-wg-add/draft-ietf-add-Encrypted-DNS-Server-RedirectionEncDNSServerRedirect/issues/4",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "mstojens",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Quoted from an email Med put to the list: \"Now that the WG finalized RESINFO spec, I think that defining attributes for associated-resolver for redirection purposes is worth to consider as well.\"",
      "createdAt": "2024-10-18T21:57:23Z",
      "updatedAt": "2024-10-18T21:57:23Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    },
    {
